{"actor": {"model": null, "profile": null, "role": "reviewer", "tool": "user"}, "at": "2026-09-18T13:00:35.567201+00:00", "event_id": "01M2T9NFVF77288FAR613P4QJB", "evidence": {"review": {"reference": "review-cycle://webkit-timing-deflake-01M2T31J/WP01-webkit-repeat-run-rig/review-cycle-2.md", "reviewer": "user", "verdict": "approved"}}, "execution_mode": "worktree", "force": true, "from_lane": "in_review", "mission_id": "01M2T31JBYZYD2AMQ16JD08Z4Y", "mission_slug": "webkit-timing-deflake-01M2T31J", "policy_metadata": {"model": null, "profile": null, "tool": "MOES-Media"}, "reason": "Review passed (--force: T005/T006a legitimately not-done, not unmet - see below). Independently verified (not self-report): all 12 canonical items covered by the rig and match real CI log 35346013373 exactly; retries=0 explicit override confirmed, 'flaky' structurally cannot appear (single-attempt runs, no retry to fold into a flaky verdict). C-009 confirmed (ci-quality.yml untouched in WP01's own 3 commits; check-gate-wiring.mjs and check-ci-quality-trigger-parity.mjs both re-run by me, exit 0). C-010 tmp/finding is a real symlink to the repo root's. T007's suppression scan verified against a REAL planted test.skip on a real spec file (not just its bundled --selftest fixtures) - caught it correctly, then cleanly reverted, tree left clean. T005/T006a: the for_review --note correctly documents both as deliberately not-done with valid reasons (T005 outside WP01's owned surface; T006a genuinely blocked - confirmed WP02-05 are still 'planned', no other WP has landed). Two non-blocking findings for the coordinator: (1) T004 was marked done with no discoverable artifact/report of which specs were checked for one-way fixture mutation - I independently audited all 5 affected spec files myself (no describe.serial/beforeAll/worker-scoped fixtures found), which supports the done conclusion substantively, but WP01 left no written trail of the check itself. (2) scan-mission-suppressions.mjs and repo